{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PREMISE CORRECTION (epic-critical; applies to whoever drives these stories). From a second epic-driver session, verified against current origin/main.\n\n## The cited corpus export no longer exists anywhere\nBoth root children quote measurements from a \"rebar export 2026-08-03\" and from session-workspace paths `files/parity_*.py`, `files/parity-results.md`, `files/rich-text-design-notes.md`. A full search found NONE of it: not on disk anywhere under the repo (including `.rebar/` and `.tickets-tracker/`), not in git history, and not in the tickets store. rebar has **no file-attachment store**, so those `files/…` paths were an ephemeral session workspace that is gone.\n\nConsequently these figures are unreproducible and unauditable, and cannot be used as ACs:\n- Cloud (`brutal-dyable-lion`): **5,730 bodies**, **99.65%** idempotent round-trip, 56.7% structurally rich, and the per-construct counts (headings 1,924; bullet lists 2,538; task lists 1,780; ordered 795; code 280; tables 60; blockquotes 33; rules 72; strong 1,396; inline-code 2,569; em 439; strike 7; link 12).\n- DC (`repressive-delectable-swan`): **179** code-arrow bodies, **70** table-erosion bodies, **~68%** of bodies / **~78%** of chars rich, the \"9115->9110 monotonic decay\" body.\n\n## The store has drifted, so the exact cardinality is unsatisfiable\nThe live store today holds **5,209** bodies, not 5,730. An AC asserting \"the fixture holds 5,730 bodies\" can never pass against a fresh export.\n\n## A vendored full corpus cannot land anyway\n`.pre-commit-config.yaml` runs `check-added-large-files` at its default **500 KB per file**; there is **no LFS**; and `.gitignore` carries a recorded decision NOT to raise that cap. The full body set is ~5.9 MB, so \"vendor the 5,730-body corpus\" is blocked by the commit gate as written.\n\n## Recommended re-scope (evidence-backed, keeps the regression value)\n1. Commit a **generator script** (doctrine already exists: `scripts/capture_jira_fixtures.py` — capture, scrub, commit, then re-assert the scrub in a test).\n2. Vendor a **stratified sample**: every body exhibiting the phenomenon under test, plus a random prose sample; shard so each file stays under 500 KB.\n3. Replace the historical cardinalities with **counts measured from the committed fixture**, asserted exactly (so a silent regeneration still fails the test), and keep the RATIO bars as floors.\n\nThis was executed for the DC side as a working reference: `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py` produces `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/{code_arrow,table,prose}.json` = 29/29/120 = **178 bodies**, each shard <=127 KB, scrub verified (0 tenant hostnames, 0 real emails, 0 live URLs). Measured over it: 92.7% of bodies / 98.4% of chars render rich. See `/tmp/pony-swan-271c.patch` and the handoff comment on `repressive-delectable-swan`.\n\nOne further caution for the Cloud story: the DC corpus run showed pandoc-class tools silently DELETE HTML comments, and rebar's own `<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->` marker is an HTML comment. Whatever engine encodes Markdown->ADF should be checked for the same class of loss before its idempotence figure is trusted."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786570478481228001,"uuid":"c58d9cfe-1f15-4b35-a040-8ddbfbb3cb0c"}